# core/data/talk/grammar/en/surf_a_flow.tlk - more replies to a plain yes, a plain no, and an
# introduction (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-SURF1, Surface push A). Content only. Clean in any room:
# no register word, no romance, no tease or blame reply, nothing aimed at the player. Kid voices are
# kid banks. Rule names start with sa_. Syntax: talkc_gen.py.

# ---- YES --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.yes.sa_back act: backchannel
  "Good. Splendid. That's the answer I was hoping for."
  "Mm-hm. A clear yes. I love a clear yes."
  "Yes, you say. Yes it is. We're in perfect agreement."
  "Right then, that settles it. Moving on, with confidence."
  "Excellent. I'll write it down. In pencil, in case you change your mind."
  "Yes, good. Now we know where we stand. Roughly here."
  "A yes, no hedging. I'm impressed. Most folks hedge."
  "Lovely. That's one thing off the list. Only forty to go."
  "Okay. Noted, stamped and filed. The cabinet's a bit full."
  "Nice and simple. If only the rest of the day were so."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_topic guard: topic act: backchannel
  "Yes to {x}! We're on the same page. A good page."
  "So it's {x}, then. Good. I'll say no more about it."
  "{x:cap}, yes. That's a good answer, and a good topic."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_morning guard: time=morning act: backchannel
  "A yes before breakfast. That's the best kind. Pure and hungry."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_night guard: time=night act: backchannel
  "A quiet yes in the dark. I like it. Very mysterious."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_happy guard: mood=happy act: backchannel
  "[HAPPY]Yes! Great! Everything's going swimmingly today!"
@rule core.yes.sa_back_tired guard: mood=tired act: backchannel
  "[SLEEPY]Yes, good. That's easy. I can manage easy today."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_polite guard: polite act: backchannel
  "Thank you for the clear answer. It's very much appreciated."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_blunt guard: blunt act: backchannel
  "Good. A yes is a yes. No need to dress it up."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_elder guard: elder act: backchannel
  "Well, that's that. In my day a yes was a handshake."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_quirky guard: quirky act: backchannel
  "Yes, hm. The sound of agreement. It's got a nice zigzag."
@rule core.yes.sa_back_flat guard: flat act: backchannel
  "Yes, okay, delighted. That's my delighted voice. Listen."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank act: thank
  "Thank you! You're a gem. A slightly dusty gem."
  "Brilliant, thanks. I knew I could count on you."
  "You said yes! I'm a lucky person. Thank you."
  "Thanks. I was nervous to ask. Now I'm only a bit nervous."
  "That's kind of you. I'll make it worth your while. Somehow."
  "Thanks a lot. You've got a heart of something warm."
  "Aw, thanks. It's good to know someone's on board."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "Thanks, friend. I knew you'd say yes. I even bet on it."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_best guard: rel=best act: thank
  "Of course you said yes. You always do. Thank you."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_family guard: rel=family act: thank
  "Thank you, love. That's family for you. Always game."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_stranger guard: rel=stranger act: thank
  "Oh, thanks! You've only just met me, and you said yes. Brave."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_sad guard: mood=sad act: thank
  "[SAD]Thank you. A yes is just what I needed today."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Thank you, dear. Such good manners. It's rare these days."
@rule core.yes.sa_thank_topic guard: topic act: thank
  "Thank you. Yes to {x} is the best yes I've had all week."
@rule core.yes.sa_joke act: joke
  "A yes! Put it in the newspaper. Page one, above the fold."
  "You said yes! Quick, say it again before you change your mind."
  "Yes. The second best word in the language. The first is cake."
  "Yes, you say! And yet the fog says maybe. We'll see who wins."
  "Wonderful. Now I'm legally allowed to be smug. Hold on, getting smug."
  "A yes! Hang on, I'll record it. For later, when you say no."
  "That's a yes with a capital Y. Or a lowercase y. I couldn't hear."
  "Yes, you absolute champion. Don't tell the others. They'd want one."
@rule core.yes.sa_joke_night guard: time=night act: joke
  "A yes at this hour? You're braver than the bats."
@rule core.yes.sa_joke_flat guard: flat act: joke
  "Yes. Hooray. I've thrown a small party in my head."
@rule core.yes.sa_agree act: agree
  "Yes, indeed. We think alike. It's a bit frightening."
  "Me too! Yes, that makes two yeses. A quorum."
  "Same here. Yes, yes, a thousand times, yes. Well, three."
  "Right? That's what I think, too. It's a good thing to think."
  "Yes. Absolutely. I'd put it on a banner."
  "We're agreed, then. It's very pleasant. Let's do it more."
@rule core.yes.sa_agree_topic guard: topic act: agree
  "Yes! {x:cap}, always. We have excellent taste."
  "Absolutely, {x} is the answer. It's the answer to nearly everything."
@rule core.yes.sa_agree_stance guard: stance=pro act: agree
  "Yes! You like it too! I'd hoped you did."
@rule core.yes.sa_agree_stance_con guard: stance=con act: agree
  "Yes, thank goodness. I wasn't sure it was just me."
@rule core.yes.sa_kid_thank guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Yay! You said yes! You're the best grown-up ever!"
  "Thank you thank you! I'll tell everyone you're nice!"
  "Yes, really? I'm going to dance now! This is the dance!"
@rule core.yes.sa_kid_back guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: backchannel
  "Okay, yes, good! Let's go, I'm ready! Are you ready?"
  "Yes! Yes yes yes! That's my favourite word!"
@rule core.yes.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "You said yes! Now you have to give me a pony! A small one!"
  "Yes, yes! Yes, I'm a yes-machine! Beep boop yes!"
@rule core.yes.sa_kid_agree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "Yes, me too! We agree! That's the best!"

# ---- NO -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.no.sa_back act: backchannel
  "Right, a no. That's fine. No is a perfectly good answer."
  "Okay. No, then. I'll cross it off, gently."
  "Fair enough. I'd rather a plain no than a polite maybe."
  "Understood. No it is. I'll sleep on it, and then forget."
  "Mm, a no. Honesty's a rare treat. Thank you."
  "No, okay. We'll try something else. There's always something else."
  "Got it. No. I'll make a note, and a cup of tea."
  "That's a firm no. I respect firm. It's a nice texture."
  "No problem. Not everything's for everyone. Even soup."
  "Okay, scratch that. Next idea. I have forty."
@rule core.no.sa_back_topic guard: topic act: backchannel
  "No to {x}? Understood. We'll never speak of it."
  "Not {x}, then. That's fine. Plenty of other things."
  "Okay, no {x}. I'll cross it off the menu."
@rule core.no.sa_back_morning guard: time=morning act: backchannel
  "A morning no. Brave. Most people wait for lunch."
@rule core.no.sa_back_night guard: time=night act: backchannel
  "A night no. It echoes, a bit. I like it."
@rule core.no.sa_back_sad guard: mood=sad act: backchannel
  "[SAD]Okay, no, it's all right. I'll cope. I usually do."
@rule core.no.sa_back_polite guard: polite act: backchannel
  "Of course. No offence taken. I appreciate your honesty."
@rule core.no.sa_back_blunt guard: blunt act: backchannel
  "Fine. No, next topic. I've got a list."
@rule core.no.sa_back_elder guard: elder act: backchannel
  "Well, that's that. A no's a no, I always say."
@rule core.no.sa_back_easygoing guard: easygoing act: backchannel
  "Sure, no, no big deal. The sun's still up. Probably."
@rule core.no.sa_complain act: complain
  "Oh, great. A no. And I was so hopeful, too."
  "You're no fun today. I'll write it in my diary."
  "No? Just no? Not even a small maybe, with sprinkles?"
  "That's disappointing. I had a speech, and everything."
  "I put on my good shirt for this. For a no."
  "Honestly. A no. In this economy."
  "Fine. No. But I'll be thinking about it all night, loudly."
@rule core.no.sa_complain_tired guard: mood=tired act: complain
  "[SLEEPY]Ugh. A no. Another thing I've got to carry to bed."
@rule core.no.sa_complain_angry guard: mood=angry act: complain
  "[ANGRY]No?! Great, that's what I expected! Marvellous!"
@rule core.no.sa_complain_friend guard: rel=friend act: complain
  "Aw, come on. You, saying no? I thought we were pals."
@rule core.no.sa_complain_best guard: rel=best act: complain
  "No, from you? I'm shocked, I'll recover. With cake."
@rule core.no.sa_complain_elder guard: elder act: complain
  "No, hm? Young people. Everything's a no, nowadays."
@rule core.no.sa_complain_topic guard: topic act: complain
  "You don't want {x}? Everyone wants {x}. Or they say they do."
@rule core.no.sa_joke act: joke
  "No, right. I'll just pretend you said yes. Works for me."
  "A no, splendid. I'll put it with the other no's. It's a big pile."
  "No? That's what the last three people said. We're a trend."
  "Noted. No, now I'll wait until you change your mind. Back soon."
  "A flat no! Like a pancake. I respect it, I'd also eat it."
  "I'd like to appeal. The court of me rules in my favour."
  "No is a complete sentence. Mine usually have more words."
  "That's a no with confidence. Frame it. Hang it by the door."
@rule core.no.sa_joke_night guard: time=night act: joke
  "A no in the dark. How ominous. Did the lamp flicker?"
@rule core.no.sa_joke_flat guard: flat act: joke
  "No, oh well. Crushed, this is my crushed face. It's flat."
@rule core.no.sa_disagree act: disagree
  "Now, hang on. I think you'd like it, if you gave it a chance."
  "No, I'd say yes. We can argue about it. I love arguing."
  "Hm, I think that's wrong. Politely, I mean. Not rudely."
  "You can say no. I'll say maybe. We'll see who wears out first."
  "I disagree with the no. I'm entitled. It's the town charter."
  "That's a bold no. I'd reconsider, take your time. I'll hum."
@rule core.no.sa_disagree_pro guard: stance=pro act: disagree
  "No? But I love it! It's one of my best things!"
@rule core.no.sa_disagree_topic guard: topic act: disagree
  "No to {x}? I'd say it deserves a second look."
@rule core.no.sa_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "No, wrong. Think again. I'll wait here with my arms crossed."
@rule core.no.sa_disagree_polite guard: polite act: disagree
  "I understand. I'd gently encourage you to reconsider, though."
@rule core.no.sa_kid_back guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: backchannel
  "Oh, okay. No, that's okay. Can we do something else?"
  "Okay! No, I'll find a different thing! I have lots!"
@rule core.no.sa_kid_complain guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "Awwww. No, I wanted yes. Yes is more fun than no."
  "No, that's not fair! I asked nicely! With a please!"
  "But why no, I'll be good! I'll be so good! Super good!"
@rule core.no.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "No, okay! No, that's the funniest word! No, no, no!"
  "Nope-nope-nope! That's a good no! I can do it too!"
@rule core.no.sa_kid_disagree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
  "No, but it's super fun! You'd love it! Try it, please?"

# ---- INTRODUCE: "I'm ..." ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet act: greet
  "Nice to meet you! Welcome. The kettle's on, the ghost isn't."
  "Hello! A pleasure. I'd say I'd heard of you, but I hadn't."
  "Well met! Come in, sit down, mind the second chair, it's wonky."
  "Hi there! I'm glad you stopped by. It's a quiet street."
  "Ah, so that's your name. I'll try to remember it. Probably."
  "Welcome to the neighbourhood. It's strange, but the soup's good."
  "Lovely to meet you. I'll introduce you to the cat. She's picky."
  "Hello! You've got a good name. It's got a nice shape."
  "Pleased to meet you. Don't worry, I only bite on Tuesdays."
  "A new face! I'll tell the others. They'll want to look."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_morning guard: time=morning act: greet
  "Morning! And a new name already. It's shaping up to be a good day."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_night guard: time=night act: greet
  "Hello, night visitor! I'm up, too. What brings you here?"
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_first guard: first act: greet
  "Hello, you! We've not met, so I'm already fond. It's a rule."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_happy guard: mood=happy act: greet
  "[HAPPY]Hello! What a lovely thing, meeting someone new!"
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_tired guard: mood=tired act: greet
  "[SLEEPY]Hello, nice to meet you. Excuse the yawning. It's not you."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_polite guard: polite act: greet
  "How do you do? It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_blunt guard: blunt act: greet
  "Right. Hi, I'm busy, but I'll make time. Briefly."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_elder guard: elder act: greet
  "Oh, how nice, a young face. Come sit, I'll tell you everything."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_quirky guard: quirky act: greet
  "I'll remember that. I write names on the inside of my hat."
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_loud guard: loud act: greet
  "HELLO, nICE TO MEET YOU! I'M A BIT LOUD! IT'S MY CHARM!"
@rule core.introduce.sa_greet_serious guard: serious act: greet
  "Good to meet you. I'm glad you've introduced yourself properly."
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask act: ask_about
  "Nice to meet you! What brings you to town? Business, soup?"
  "Pleasure! So, what do you do? Besides introducing yourself."
  "Hello! Are you new here, or just new to me?"
  "Lovely! Tell me about yourself. Start with your favourite thing."
  "Ah, hello, where do you live? Near the fountain? The graveyard?"
  "Welcome! What's your story? I'll bring tea, you bring drama."
  "Well hello. What's the most interesting thing about you? I'm listening."
  "Nice name. Does it have a story? Names usually do."
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask_topic guard: topic act: ask_about
  "Pleased to meet you! Are you into {x}? Everyone round here is."
  "Hello! I'd love to hear what you think about {x}."
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask_first guard: first act: ask_about
  "Hello! I don't know you, which means there's loads to learn."
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask_friend guard: rel=friend act: ask_about
  "Hi, again! You introduce yourself every time. I like it."
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask_polite guard: polite act: ask_about
  "Delighted. Might I ask what brings you to our little corner?"
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask_elder guard: elder act: ask_about
  "Oh, hello, dear. Who are your people? I might know them."
@rule core.introduce.sa_ask_quirky guard: quirky act: ask_about
  "Hello! What's your favourite colour? It tells me everything."
@rule core.introduce.sa_joke act: joke
  "I'm delighted to meet you. I'm sure we'll be great friends. Or neighbours."
  "Pleased to meet you! I'd shake your hand, but it's in the soup."
  "Nice to meet you! I'm a legend in my own mind. Pleased to make it two."
  "Introductions! How formal. I'll bring the good biscuits."
  "A new name! Quick, I need to forget it so I can ask again."
  "That's a fine name. I'd steal it, but it wouldn't fit."
  "Ooh, an introduction. Do I curtsy? I'm going to curtsy."
  "A pleasure, don't mind the mess. It's not mine. Probably."
@rule core.introduce.sa_joke_night guard: time=night act: joke
  "A new name after dark. Mysterious. Do you have a cape?"
@rule core.introduce.sa_joke_flat guard: flat act: joke
  "Hello. I'm thrilled to meet you. That was my thrilled voice."
@rule core.introduce.sa_kid_greet guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: greet
  "Hi, I'm a kid! You're a grown-up! We can be friends!"
  "Hello, nice to meet you! Do you like frogs? I love frogs!"
  "Hi hi hi, your name's cool! Mine's cooler! No, just as cool!"
@rule core.introduce.sa_kid_ask guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: ask_about
  "Hi! What's your favourite animal? Mine's a snail!"
  "Hello, do you have a pet? I want a pet dragon! A small one!"
  "Nice to meet you! Can you do a cartwheel? I can do half."
@rule core.introduce.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "Hello, I'm the best at hi! Hi hi! That was three hi's!"
  "Nice to meet you! I'd shake your hand but it's sticky!"
